# Thur VTL — daemon environment file
#
# Loaded by the systemd unit at startup
# (`EnvironmentFile=-/etc/thurvtl/thurvtl.env`) and exposed to the
# daemon process. The leading `-` in the unit makes this file
# optional — if every env var the daemon needs comes from
# elsewhere (cloud VM instance identity, an external secrets
# manager, etc.), leave the file empty or absent.
#
# Anything the daemon needs in its environment goes here:
#   - Cloud-provider credentials (AWS / GCS / Azure access keys).
#   - Secrets referenced from thurvtl.yaml via ${ENV_VAR}
#     interpolation (alerting webhook tokens, SMTP passwords,
#     etc.).
#   - Future feature flags / debug toggles that take the form of
#     env vars.
#
# Full reference for cloud authentication — when to use this file
# vs. per-backend `auth:` blocks in thurvtl.yaml, multi-provider
# layouts, and the precedence rules — is in the project's
# docs/AUTH.md (Thur VTL source repository).
#
# Quick rules:
#   - Single-provider on-prem: drop the env vars below into this
#     file and you're done.
#   - Multi-provider (multiple S3-flavored backends): the AWS chain
#     is process-global, so put per-backend `auth:` blocks in
#     thurvtl.yaml instead — see AUTH.md.
#   - Cloud VM with instance identity: leave the cloud section
#     empty; the provider's SDK picks up creds automatically.
#
# File format: one KEY=VALUE per line. No `export`. No quotes
# around values (systemd parses the line as-is). Lines starting
# with `#` are comments.
#
# Permissions: this file ships as root:thurvtl 0640 — readable
# by the daemon's group, opaque to other users. After editing,
# `systemctl restart thurvtld` to pick up changes.

# -- AWS S3 / MinIO / Wasabi --------------------------------------
# Long-lived IAM access key. Prefer an EC2 instance profile or
# IRSA on EKS where available (no static credentials on disk).
#AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
#AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
#AWS_REGION=us-east-1
# Optional: short-lived STS session token (set alongside the
# access key + secret when assuming a role).
#AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=
# Optional: select a named profile from ~/.aws/credentials instead
# of using the access key / secret above.
#AWS_PROFILE=

# -- Google Cloud Storage -----------------------------------------
# Path to a service-account JSON key file. Lock it down the same
# way as this file (root:thurvtl 0640). On GCE / GKE the
# metadata server is used automatically — leave commented.
#GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/etc/thurvtl/gcs-sa.json

# -- Azure Blob Storage -------------------------------------------
# The daemon picks the first auth method that has its env vars
# set, in this order: SAS URL > shared key > AAD service principal
# (and falls through to Managed Identity / az CLI when none are
# set). Pick ONE block.
#
# (a) SAS URL (full container or account URL with SAS token):
#AZURE_STORAGE_SAS_URL=
#
# (b) Shared key:
#AZURE_STORAGE_KEY=
#
# (c) AAD service principal:
#AZURE_TENANT_ID=
#AZURE_CLIENT_ID=
#AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET=
